{"algorithm":"ML-KEM","schema":"mlkem_test_schema.json","numberOfTests":200,"notes":{"Strcmp":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"In ML-KEM.Decaps the ciphertext is compared with the output of K-PKE.Encrypt for implicit rejection. If an implementation were to use strcmp() for that comparison it would fail to reject some ciphertexts if a zero byte terminates the comparison early. The chance of it occurring randomly is 2⁻¹⁶. These vectors are valid and test that the implicit rejection path is taken as expected."},"MalleableCiphertext":{"bugType":"CAN_OF_WORMS","description":"The ciphertext is malleable."}},"testGroups":[{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"CCTV/strcmp","version":"0.1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-512","tests":[{"tcId":1,"flags":["Strcmp"],"seed":"a3896e30892230a6c1dff667f8caee759ff84a08e3462ae484fcbca9971d7959cdc6c5ec65f10a5a24b5145aac863232ee3b2229ca3a6c4b9c8a2dafc315d9d4","ek":"","c":"","K":"cf3bcfeb2679cb43658fcdcd01aa1505bcea1e72a165ccac7bfb66d9dc0c0e90","result":"valid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"FIPS 203","version":"1.0"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-512","tests":[{"tcId":2,"comment":"Test vector based on official round 3 seeds 0","flags":[],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694aa0c6d10e4db6b1add2fd81a25ccb148032dcd739936737f2d8626ed79d451140800e03b59b956f8210e556067407d13dc90fa9e8b872bfb8f","ek":"","c":"","K":"319839e82ab6b222de7b619e80da8391522bbb37677018494a4742c53f9abfdf","result":"valid"},{"tcId":102,"comment":"Private key too short","flags":[],"seed":"ca04150eedf8e034220dad06ffc82e27a2ddccb0e48644f0d536b2044b9fa623b96f","c":"","K":"","result":"invalid"}]},{"type":"MLKEMTest","source":{"name":"github.com/007bsd/mlkem-implicit-rejection","version":"1"},"parameterSet":"ML-KEM-512","tests":[{"tcId":194,"comment":"Ciphertext modified at byte 0 (c1 poly-block 0); implicit rejection must fire, so a re-encryption comparison that skips this position is detected","flags":["MalleableCiphertext"],"seed":"7c9935a0b07694aa0c6d10e4db6b1add2fd81a25ccb148032dcd7